module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.nominal_isomorphic_record_admitted_at_sibling_declaration

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { AtCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import std.decl_ref { decl_ref }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }

data nominal_isomorphic_record_admitted_at_sibling_declaration: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "nominal_isomorphic_record_admitted_at_sibling_declaration" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: StructurallyGuaranteed }, standing: AtCeiling { rung: StructurallyGuaranteed, ceiling_reason: "THE CLIMBED PATH (the judgment), on executed evidence. The judgment derives the refusal from modeled structure: the call's own solved map keys the declared identity at the generic-formal slot, executed RED (EXIT 0, accepted+evaluated, on main -- src/v1/stage0/tests/nominal_isomorphic_record_admission.rs on the production CLI route) to GREEN (a typed refusal naming both declarations) at this head, with the same-nominal and direct-slot positive controls holding -- DESIGN section 4b rung 3: the invalid state stays describable but no Accepted program contains it. RUNG 4 IS THIS CLASS'S CEILING-BOUNDARY, NOT ITS STATE: two record declarations with matching field shapes are writable by the language's own design (that is what a structural record is), so no constructor removal makes the field-isomorphic sibling unreachable -- rung 3 (compiler refuses) is the highest rung the class can hold, and it holds it. THE SPLIT THE REVIEW NAMES: the rung reports the CLIMBED generic-formal judgment path only; the unjudged population the flip merely EXPOSED (the String-typed builtin concat at List-typed formals) is a separate still-open class, recorded on the remaining-population receipt below with its own closing capability, and does not lower this rung." as NonEmptyStr } },

  receipts: [
    "**a nominal record admitted at a field-isomorphic sibling declaration** (invalid state: a value of one declared nominal record type reaches a slot whose declared type is a DIFFERENT nominal record type with the same field names and types, and the front end accepts it because the check that fires compares STRUCTURE -- field labels and types -- where the declaration's IDENTITY decides. The two declarations are one fact restated twice (DESIGN section 3's nickname fork at the type layer), so nothing the structure check can see distinguishes them; the first refusal happens in the emitted target, where distinct Rust structs make the mismatch a compile error. Harm: DESIGN section 4b(1)'s rung below the ladder -- a value not inhabiting its declared type passes as Accepted, so the ladder's verdict is reported green while rustc, not gunbc, is the authority that judges inhabitance).",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: a value at its OWN declaration with matching structure is not this class (that is ordinary inhabitance); a subtype or widening coercion admitted by a cited law is not this class (that is an authority, not an absence of one); a structural comparison is legitimate WHERE the specification declared it structural (a structural record type, a canonical-form comparison) -- this class is structural comparison at a slot whose declared type is a NOMINAL record, where identity decides. The tell is the pair: nominal declaration at the slot AND a judgment that cannot see the declaration's identity.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: WHERE A SLOT DECLARES A NOMINAL RECORD TYPE, INHABITANCE IS DECIDED BY THE RESOLVED DECLARATION IDENTITY OF THE VALUE'S TYPE -- FIELD SHAPE MAY ONLY JOIN TWO NODES AFTER THE HEADS ARE THE SAME DECLARATION. A field-isomorphic sibling MUST NOT inhabit: a value not inhabiting its declared type is a refusal at the earliest producer, never a pass to rustc.",

    "REMAINING LATENT POPULATION, recorded so it is not silently left. The four map_insert value sites this row's judgment flip exposed and migrated were not the whole population of one builtin's misuse: a grep sizing (a sizing ESTIMATE from a textual match, NOT an instrument census -- it counts source occurrences, not resolvable call sites, and does not distinguish a List-typed formal from a String one) found the pattern concat(xs, [item]) -- a list concatenated with a singleton, the shape the String-typed builtin concat is misused for while the interpreter's concat happens to also handle lists -- occurring 1560 times across 643 source files. Only the sites inside the heal-candidate resolve closure are checked by this row's judgment; the rest stay latent, invisible until each enters a resolve that judges its formal's declared type. THE CAPABILITY THAT WOULD CLOSE IT: the instrument v2-native-census-scoped walking the full corpus under the corrected judgment (a per-site inhabitance census), turning this grep estimate into an executed count and a per-site disposition; until then the class stays open and this estimate is the only record of its size.",

    "Rung found at: below the ladder (DESIGN 4b(1): the front end accepted; the emitted target refused). Mitigatable: no -- the acceptance is exactly what the ladder is for; the ceiling is the fix at the judgment link (a head-identity gate before the structural comparison of a nominal pair, refusing with a typed cause naming both declarations), plus deleting the nickname pair so one declaration remains.",

    "RECEIPT 2026-10-20 (quiet-carp-503, tidy-ant-251's brief; found while routing the census occurrence-identity PR #14574, whose deviation exposed it). PRODUCER: v2.compiler.reference_conservation refusal_cover_add (:531-538) snocs the literal `ByteRange { start: s, end: e }` (ByteRange: v2.std.diagnostic :10, a variant `| ByteRange { start: Int, end: Int }` of the Locus Extent coproduct) into `ranges: FreeMonoid<RefusalRange>` (RefusalCover.ranges, :518) where `type RefusalRange { start: Int, end: Int }` (:511) is a structural nickname of ByteRange. rustc is the FIRST refusal: E0308 at emitted v2_compiler_reference_conservation.rs:375, when the module first entered the v2-native-census-scoped emitted closure (import of the census keying rule) -- the census run exited 2 there, measured 2026-10-20, while the same census without that import emits clean. The emitter was verified FAITHFUL (clever-crane-830's correction, confirmed at the source): it rendered the source's literal; the defect is the front end admitting a value that does not inhabit its declared element type, plus the nickname. STAGE: INFER admits it (resolve passes; the accept is at src/v1/04_infer.dag, emitted twin v1_compiler_infer.rs): direct_call_argument_inhabitance_diags (:6051) builds the PositionDirectCallArgument obligation with declared := the formal's substitution_basis whenever the formal carries an unbound TypeVariable (:6179), and declared_type_inhabitance (:4433) diverts every generic formal to InhabitanceUndecidable { reason: UndecidableGenericFormal } at :4458 -- EARLIER than every head-identity gate. Undecidable is advisory and never blocking (:5300-5318, is_interpreter_blocking_diagnostic), so the call is silently Accepted: the item:T formal binds T to the sibling record with zero obligations, and the monomorphic container field is a separate obligation on a separate formal that nothing compares against the T-binding. THE WORKING GATE EXISTS AND IS MADE UNREACHABLE: nominal_product_inhabitance_refusal (:4909) head-differ -> RefusedDistinctProductConstructor is exactly what refuses the same pair at a DIRECT (non-generic) slot (measured refusal: \"value does not inhabit its declared type at the direct call argument for parameter r: declared Product(RefusalRange), produced Product(OtherRange)\"); :4458 diverts generic formals before it is consulted. The defect is therefore the ORDERING of the wholesale Undecidable diversion ahead of an existing identity gate, not a missing comparison. THE v2 RELATION IS EXONERATED BY MEASUREMENT: the self-contained v2-DAG route (assemble_program_from_ingest over the production closure) REFUSES this pair with application_argument_does_not_inhabit -- the divergence is v1-only, so no coordination with the v2 inhabitance lane (jolly-bee-729's #14516 chain, sharp-ram-803's infer.dag work) is required. FIX (ruled by tidy-ant-251, 2026-10-20): the generic formal's substituted pair is judged with the call's OWN solved substitution map (the one unification produced -- no second solver, no re-derivation) through the existing nominal_product_inhabitance_refusal; UndecidableGenericFormal stays only for a variable genuinely unsolved after the call. This also closes the first-occurrence-binding gap as ONE RULE, which is the stated reason the unification-site alternative was NOT taken (DESIGN 3b, stated divergence): every argument at a T-typed position is judged against the substituted formal, which is exactly the consistency check a second gate at unify would have added -- a second check would be a second producer of the same verdict. Admission purpose of the v1 seed change (gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing): it closes a silent accept the v2 relation already refuses, so the corpus stops relying on the seed admitting it. RED: src/v1/stage0/tests/nominal_isomorphic_record_admission.rs on the production CLI route -- on main the real-producer shape and the local generic-formal shape EXIT 0 (accepted, evaluated), while the same-nominal controls and the direct-slot refusal control PASS.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "direct_call_argument_inhabitance_diags"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v2.compiler.reference_conservation", decl_name: "range_encloses_atom"),
  ],
}
